From 97616b6d08fe3eef2165ecdc23cb6a03912dc0cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:51:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 093/113] rust: usb: manage I/O windows in the driver adapter

USB transfers are only permitted between probe or resume and the matching suspend, reset, or disconnect callback. IoWindow represented that interval, but each driver had to construct it unsafely and remember every lifecycle transition.

Have the USB adapter own the window and pass a reference-counted handle to probe. Add a quiesce callback so drivers can stop producers before the adapter closes and drains the window. Reopen it before resume callbacks and close it again if resume fails.

Convert Vino and the USB sample. Vino no longer constructs, closes, or reopens its I/O capability itself.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
---
 rust/kernel/usb.rs              | 133 ++++++++++++++++++++------------
 samples/rust/rust_driver_usb.rs |   6 +-
 2 files changed, 87 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rust/kernel/usb.rs b/rust/kernel/usb.rs
index d24abcefa93a..5d7f6e130c43 100644
--- a/rust/kernel/usb.rs
+++ b/rust/kernel/usb.rs
